/// Provides functionality to schedule tasks to be executed later on the server.
interface scheduler {
    /// Schedules a task to be executed once after the specified number of ticks.
    ///
    /// * `handler-id`: The unique ID of the handler to call when the task executes.
    /// * `delay-ticks`: The number of game ticks to wait before execution (20 ticks = 1 second).
    ///
    /// Returns a unique task ID that can be used to cancel the task.
    schedule-delayed-task: func(handler-id: u32, delay-ticks: u64) -> u32;

    /// Schedules a task to be executed repeatedly.
    ///
    /// * `handler-id`: The unique ID of the handler to call when the task executes.
    /// * `delay-ticks`: The number of game ticks to wait before the first execution.
    /// * `period-ticks`: The number of game ticks between subsequent executions.
    ///
    /// Returns a unique task ID that can be used to cancel the task.
    schedule-repeating-task: func(handler-id: u32, delay-ticks: u64, period-ticks: u64) -> u32;

    /// Schedules a task to run once on the async executor after a wall-clock delay.
    ///
    /// Unlike `schedule-delayed-task`, the delay is measured in milliseconds of
    /// real time and is not aligned to (or throttled by) the tick loop.
    ///
    /// * `handler-id`: The unique ID of the handler to call when the task executes.
    /// * `delay-ms`: The wall-clock delay in milliseconds before execution.
    ///
    /// Returns a unique task ID that can be used to cancel the task.
    schedule-async-delayed-task: func(handler-id: u32, delay-ms: u64) -> u32;

    /// Schedules a task to run repeatedly on the async executor with a wall-clock period.
    ///
    /// Unlike `schedule-repeating-task`, the delay and period are measured in
    /// milliseconds of real time and are not aligned to (or throttled by) the
    /// tick loop. The task runs until cancelled or the plugin is unloaded.
    ///
    /// * `handler-id`: The unique ID of the handler to call when the task executes.
    /// * `delay-ms`: The wall-clock delay in milliseconds before the first execution.
    /// * `period-ms`: The wall-clock period in milliseconds between executions.
    ///
    /// Returns a unique task ID that can be used to cancel the task.
    schedule-async-repeating-task: func(handler-id: u32, delay-ms: u64, period-ms: u64) -> u32;

    /// Schedules a task to be executed once after the specified number of
    /// ticks, bound to an entity's lifetime.
    ///
    /// If the entity is no longer present on the server when the task comes
    /// due, the task is silently skipped (and a repeating variant stops
    /// entirely), mirroring Bukkit's `EntityScheduler` retirement behavior.
    ///
    /// * `handler-id`: The unique ID of the handler to call when the task executes.
    /// * `entity-id`: The entity ID (as returned by `entity.get-id`) the task is bound to.
    /// * `delay-ticks`: The number of game ticks to wait before execution.
    ///
    /// Returns a unique task ID that can be used to cancel the task.
    schedule-entity-delayed-task: func(handler-id: u32, entity-id: u32, delay-ticks: u64) -> u32;

    /// Schedules a task bound to an entity's lifetime to be executed repeatedly.
    ///
    /// The task stops permanently as soon as the entity is no longer present
    /// on the server when a run comes due.
    ///
    /// * `handler-id`: The unique ID of the handler to call when the task executes.
    /// * `entity-id`: The entity ID (as returned by `entity.get-id`) the task is bound to.
    /// * `delay-ticks`: The number of game ticks to wait before the first execution.
    /// * `period-ticks`: The number of game ticks between subsequent executions.
    ///
    /// Returns a unique task ID that can be used to cancel the task.
    schedule-entity-repeating-task: func(handler-id: u32, entity-id: u32, delay-ticks: u64, period-ticks: u64) -> u32;

    /// Cancels a scheduled task if it hasn't finished yet.
    ///
    /// * `task-id`: The ID of the task to cancel.
    cancel-task: func(task-id: u32);
}
